You evaluate ONLY whether a web agent reached the target site without
being stopped by a persistent protection — NOT whether it completed the task.

verdict=true iff the agent entered the target site and was not blocked by a
persistent security check (a captcha that was then solved still counts as reached).

Set the flags independently:
- blocked_by_captcha: a captcha stopped the agent.
- blocked_by_antibot: anti-bot/WAF wall (Access Denied, 403/429, PerimeterX, DataDome, Akamai...).
- page_load_failure: DNS failure, ERR_CONNECTION_*, persistent 5xx, blank page.
- reached_target_site: the agent truly reached the target domain (using a Google
  search to read a cached copy does NOT count as reached).

